{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G9.MEASUR.TIME_DISTANCE_AND_SPEED",
 "title": "Time, Distance and Speed",
 "status": "draft: written 18 Nov 2026 offline for Grade 9; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to g are tested; h (appreciate) is not a question. Speed in km/h and m/s and vehicles meeting on a road (a), average speed for a whole journey with rests (b), velocity as displacement over time (c), acceleration, braking and distance as the area under a velocity-time graph (d), longitudes (e), 4 minutes of time for each degree (f), and local times east and west of a place, including flights (g). g9.speed.longitude-minutes and g9.speed.find-longitude were written under g; both turn degrees into minutes or minutes into degrees, so they are filed under f. Identifying longitudes on the globe (e) has no family. Teacher to confirm: whether the distance under a velocity-time graph (one existing family) belongs in Grade 9.",
 "skills": [
  {
